                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "camp",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f195f09d-1276-3134-8c30-ad9a8bd0e7ba",
                                        "entry_id": "3a431ad2-f25b-3d45-878c-b9db13ccd694",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An affected, exaggerated, or intentionally tasteless style."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d68e7853-3948-4638-9619-acda4f2cf659",
                                                "sense_id": "f195f09d-1276-3134-8c30-ad9a8bd0e7ba",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: campness, campiness"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "550304e9-58bd-470c-ba41-38c39a0911f5",
                                                "sense_id": "f195f09d-1276-3134-8c30-ad9a8bd0e7ba",
                                                "text": "We walk a fine line, just this side of camp. Careful calculations are made. We sense that while it might be wonderful for Krystle and Alexis to have a catfight in a koi pond, it would be inappropriate for Joan to smack Linda with a koi."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbd0e291-4010-4d48-be54-36280d1f75b8",
                                                "sense_id": "f195f09d-1276-3134-8c30-ad9a8bd0e7ba",
                                                "text": "Why would any Hollywood studio encourage a film's transformation into camp, in effect joining in the mockery of its own product? MGM declined to comment."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "camp",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b672e7ad-d5b0-3148-bf36-2232cbd8eee5",
                                        "entry_id": "077b18b6-ee8f-3b3d-a7c0-3f827158592a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Theatrical; making exaggerated gestures."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d0643266-3d3c-3bd1-b152-57db695809ab",
                                        "entry_id": "077b18b6-ee8f-3b3d-a7c0-3f827158592a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ostentatiously effeminate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a man"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6db688ab-7a68-43d4-aa35-b704a703d983",
                                                "sense_id": "d0643266-3d3c-3bd1-b152-57db695809ab",
                                                "text": "More recently the word has become colloquial English for either implying that someone is a homosexual (‘he's very camp’), or for describing rather outre behaviour[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80c5af74-f344-49c3-b1ca-c6616524aa2e",
                                                "sense_id": "d0643266-3d3c-3bd1-b152-57db695809ab",
                                                "text": "And to be honest, in the illustration Mr Tumnus does look as camp as fuck with his little scarf tied jauntily around his neck. I suppose it isn't outside the realms of possibility that he'd just been off cottaging with some centaurs in the forest. God."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2d857cec-ab2f-3ed9-a49e-15006efbc09a",
                                        "entry_id": "077b18b6-ee8f-3b3d-a7c0-3f827158592a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Intentionally tasteless or vulgar; self-parodying."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cfd6305b-0740-4b04-8ef7-b2b9dea8bb31",
                                                "sense_id": "2d857cec-ab2f-3ed9-a49e-15006efbc09a",
                                                "text": "In Saturday Night Live, Madonna also unsurprisingly played Princess Diana, Marilyn Monroe, and a Joan Collins clone, all in a very camp way. As John Dean writes: “U.S. rock has a ruling camp queen with Madonna.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06e71116-d82d-4e1c-8838-3e8e8b11c097",
                                                "sense_id": "2d857cec-ab2f-3ed9-a49e-15006efbc09a",
                                                "text": "Here is Eurovision from a time before anyone watched it for camp value – you can’t imagine any gay bar in 1974 clearing its schedules to screen this; a Eurovision that takes itself rather seriously, a brief appearance by the Wombles notwithstanding."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "camp",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e35c7a71-bac1-3f85-9743-9e0092a9c6e1",
                                        "entry_id": "5fbfc500-12e8-32a6-8035-b6357d366c56",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To behave in a camp manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b312d049-d64a-4059-a784-d7a6b3f750dd",
                                                "sense_id": "e35c7a71-bac1-3f85-9743-9e0092a9c6e1",
                                                "text": "Oster and his his two co-stars, Jamie MacKenzie and Bill Martel, boogie and bop, sway and swish, camp and croon through tightly worked production numbers addressing a range of serious (and not so serious) issues that middle class, urban gay men come up against."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
